<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  User-domain LaunchAgent for arkdeck-agentd.

  A Mach service exists only when launchd vends it: a daemon started straight
  from a shell has nothing to check in to, so its read-only XPC door stays
  closed and only the Unix socket serves. That is the correct configuration
  for CLI, CI and host agents, and nothing here changes it — this file exists
  for the one client that cannot use the Unix socket, the sandboxed App.

  Install (user domain, no administrator rights, fully reversible):

    cp Packages/ArkDeckKit/LaunchAgents/com.arkdeck.agentd.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    # then edit the ProgramArguments path below to the built arkdeck-agentd
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.arkdeck.agentd.plist

  Remove:

    launchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.arkdeck.agentd
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.arkdeck.agentd.plist

  The MachServices key below, ArkDeckAgentXPC.machServiceName, and the App's
  com.apple.security.temporary-exception.mach-lookup.global-name entitlement
  must all name the same service. AgentXPCTransportContractTests pins that.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.arkdeck.agentd</string>
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/usr/local/bin/arkdeck-agentd</string>
	</array>
	<key>MachServices</key>
	<dict>
		<key>com.arkdeck.agentd</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<false/>
	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Standard</string>
</dict>
</plist>
